title The card earns its own bound, and an exception nothing had tested
prompt raise the card's bound like session-logs earned its own
think session-logs earned 57,344 on two halves, and only one of them is available to the card. The half it cannot borrow is the reading: an index is read from the TOP and a bound written for a page read whole refuses it for doing its job. The card is read WHOLE, every lap, by every body -- its own seat prompts say so in those words -- so it is exactly the page 24,576 was written for. What changed is not how it is read but what it now has to hold.
think So the number is derived rather than granted, which is the half it does borrow. Measured on the card at 24,575 of 24,576: the Standing block 7,008 across 14 directives, the live front 5,161, the durable spine 12,406. Sixteen directives at 512 is 8,192 -- sixteen because fourteen stand and a power of two leaves room for two more without a rewrite; 8,192 for the live front, the same prose allowance the index earned; 16,384 for the spine, the only part with genuine slack. That is 32,768, a power of two, about 8k tokens against the general bound's 6k.
obs The cost is named in the law rather than waved past. A page read whole by six bodies costs its bytes every lap, so this is roughly two thousand tokens per lap per body and nothing recovers them. It is worth paying because the measured alternative is worse: one session condensed this card seventeen times across two laps to fit three ledger rows and a launcher, closing at one byte under the ceiling, and which prose got cut was decided by whoever happened to be typing. A pin with one byte of headroom does not bound a page, it taxes every lap a judgment call nobody asked for.
obs SHRED_PREP is deliberately NOT raised, and the law says why in the same breath: it sat at 210 bytes free the same day and was repaired by folding a completed shed's record to the archive. A finished section belongs on a shelf; only a page whose LIVING parts have outgrown the number earns a new one. Two pins, two different answers, one principle.
obs Seating the second exception immediately exposed a red the first never could. tools/fixtures/e/equinox_e123_living_pin_guard_scan.sh called the bound fixture bare, once, and measured every pin on its roster against that single answer -- so it refused the card at detail_max=24576 in the same minute the fixture answered 32768 for that page. Two meters reading one law to opposite verdicts, both sure.
obs Why eleven days passed with nothing noticing: the per-page reading was seated 20260824 with exactly one page named, and that page measures 7,817 bytes -- comfortably under the general 24,576. So every guard ignoring the per-page argument still passed it, for the wrong reason. A conditional only one input reaches has been tested by nothing, however green the tree reads. Kin to %408 in this same session, where a branch conditional on a file only the guarded process could create never ran at all: one is a branch never taken, the other a branch taken always.
obs One thing carried back out of the cairns now that there is room, and only one: the unanswered question beside %400 -- should an OPEN row carry a claim, a seat and a stamp, at start rather than at landing? Landed detail was the cheaper cut and stays cut; a question nobody has answered should not vanish because a byte ceiling squeezed it. The rest waits at its walk-back nib, which is what the cairns are for.
loom card_bytes=26176 card_bound=32768 headroom=6592 was=1
loom witness=equinox_e123 planted_over=32769 refused=yes prove_red=refuses
loom roster=standing_equipment hot=1 guards=111 green=107 red=0 gated=4 wall_s=1607 verdict=ok receipt=written
loom roster=standing_equipment scoped=1 basis=1565a388bd changed=6 skipped=33
obs The first fully passing close on this clone: 111 run, 107 green, ZERO red, four gated, run_verdict=ok, and the receipt written for the first time -- carrying gated 4 and naming all four gates inside itself, which is what %374 promised rather than a bare green. Before the word that receipt was unreachable BY CONSTRUCTION here, since every full pass closed guard_red on gates that are permanent by design.
obs And the thing the word actually bought, proven on metal rather than argued: a --scoped pass read the basis, saw six changed files, and skipped 33 guards it could prove unaffected. That is the fusion build's cheaper pass running for the first time on this pier.
file context/specs/20260724-132812_pin-and-ledger-living-pin-max-bytes.md the second exception, derived from the card's own three measured parts, with the per-lap cost named
file tools/fixtures/e/equinox_e123_living_pin_guard_scan.sh the scan asks the bound fixture per page inside its loop and prints pin_max beside every pin_ok
file construction/REDS.md %410 -- an exception no guard had been asked to honor, because the one page carrying it never needed it
file construction/ITINERARY.md its own bound named in its header, with the derivation and the general bound both stated
recommend kg -- the raise is seated and proven from both sides; the fold and the near-bound advisory both still stand for the next pin that fills
